<Layout
    title="About Me"
    description="about joshua and who he is as a person"
    hero={"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Joshua_Commanding_the_Sun_to_Stand_Still_upon_Gibeon_%281816%29_John_Martin_-_NGA_2004.64.1.jpg/2560px-Joshua_Commanding_the_Sun_to_Stand_Still_upon_Gibeon_%281816%29_John_Martin_-_NGA_2004.64.1.jpg"}
>
    <section class="about">
        <p>
            I love quite mornings and late nights when everyone else is fast
            asleep.
        </p>
        <p>
            I spend much of my time tinkering with computers, reading, watching
            films, and following curiosities wherever they happen to lead.
        </p>
        <p>Lately, that has meant building this digital garden.</p>

        <p>
            I work primarily on Linux, I use Arch btw. I enjoy setting up small
            systems for myself like media libraries, personal tools, servers,
            webDAVs and experiments that don’t need an audience. <br /> Not everything
            has to scale, ship or perform. Some things are allowed to exist simply
            because they are useful or comforting. <br />
            But I feel they do deserve to be jotted down somewhere, on what they were
            ment to be and what they have become and why. <br />
            This is where most of them are explained.
        </p>

        <p>
            If you’ve found your way here, you’re welcome to linger. This space
            isn’t meant to impress. It’s an attempt to make something honest,
            and to invite you, into the gentle disorder of my thinking.
        </p>
    </section>
</Layout>
